<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Front for the Restoration of Unity and Democracy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1991–present</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as FRUD</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Front for the Restoration of Unity and Democracy (FRUD) is a political movement of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afar">Afar</a> people of Djibouti, formed in 1991. It launched an armed rebellion that year against the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hassan-gouled-aptidon">Hassan Gouled Aptidon</a>, protesting at the dominance of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/issa-clan">Issa Somali</a>. A peace accord in 1994 brought its main wing into government, and a radical faction fought on until agreements of 2000 and 2001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/front-for-the-restoration-of-unity-and-democracy.jpg" alt="Front for the Restoration of Unity and Democracy" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Front_for_the_Restoration_of_Unity_and_Democracy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
